<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Turkey to push for 'electrification' drive at COP31 as climate threats mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01fb40f075a1c5429106542f41e3f92eda781c6515c07536511bc8d0981db8d6</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T15:36:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261106-turkey-to-push-for-electrification-drive-at-cop31-as-climate-threats-mount" /><summary type="html">COP31 host Turkey is set to push for a "electrification" drive to help meet global elergy demand as the UN climate conference kicks off in Antalya on Monday. The annual summit takes place this year under the shadow of a cost-of-living crisis fuelled by the war in the Middle East.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>China keeps a close eye on US midterm shake-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:124b670eaea295fb0b4ec0e7b93e92049afd26be0f03d1111cbdac3293333a86</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T15:03:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261106-china-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-shake-up" /><summary type="html">The US midterm elections have resulted in the Democratic Party taking control of both chambers of the US Congress, leaving Donald Trump as a lame duck president for the remainder of his term. Professor Steve Tsang of the SOAS China Institute tells FRANCE 24 that, while a weakened Trump could strengthen Beijing's negotiating position, the Chinese leadership is aware that Congress has relatively little sway over foreign policy and is keen to maintain warm personal ties between the two presidents.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo embarks on Latin America trip with a first stop in Uruguay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:960881f5b0c748a5dce48ed41578a4d88281adab0a9f4a6eb4d98c9431e34715</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:58:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-pope-leo-embarks-on-latin-america-trip-with-a-first-stop-in-uruguay" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV is kicking off a three-nation tour of Latin America on Friday, November 6, with a visit to Uruguay, the region’s least Catholic and most secular country, three weeks after undergoing lung cancer surgery that had put the entire trip into question. After Uruguay, he will then go to Argentina and Peru. FRANCE 24's Hanna Roberts has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>California governor to grant clemency to all 548 death row inmates in state</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f47709a5511dbea2370c4b007c6731a762e151bc67ff1a841333355f0d22ed54</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:54:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-california-governor-to-grant-clemency-to-all-548-death-row-inmates-in-state" /><summary type="html">California's governor Gavy Newsom announced Thursday that he will commute all death sentences in the state to life without the possibility of parole. He said that "capital punishment is morally wrong." The state Supreme Court will have the final say in hundreds of those cases.</summary></entry><entry><title>The women who rode the blue wave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21b71cee4643efac395ec4895b751a1ad474332b11968204c105929265549e29</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:15:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261106-the-women-who-rode-the-blue-wave" /><summary type="html">In this edition, we report on how the US midterms, which saw the Democrats make massive gains, also marked a series of historic firsts for women. Also the dark side to Bangkok's booming fertility industry, which attracts thousands of foreign patients seeking assistance from the Thai capital's state-of-the-art private clinics. Plus how an impoverished neighbourhood in El Salvador, once a no-go zone plagued by gang violence, is being transformed by women into a vibrant canvas for street art.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>'Too early to draw conclusions' as bomb threat hoaxes target European countries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b945391840ced9fbacf11e3eefd7ab4342239fe487ec81548d8bfd09d62531d2</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:48:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-too-early-to-draw-conclusions-as-bomb-threat-hoaxes-target-european-countries" /><summary type="html">Several Irish media outlets reported receiving bomb threats on Friday as a wave of hoax alerts that had so far mainly targeted airlines continued across Europe, with more than a dozen new flights affected. No explosives have been found in any of the incidents so far. European authorities are scrambling to identify the sources of the threats, as FRANCE 24's Brussels correspondent Dave Keating reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paraguay's Peña offers resignation amid banking scandal, protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e8e9a754d9a220b0a7678ef4537b35e552ed459dcf65b697993d1eb01555804</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:45:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-paraguay-s-pe%C3%B1a-offers-resignation-amid-banking-scandal-protests" /><summary type="html">Paraguayan President Santiago Peña submitted his resignation on Thursday, but Congress put it on hold as impeachment proceedings against him move forward. Peña is facing impeachment over a banking scandal that has affected millions of people and sparked protests, with thousands taking to the streets in recent days.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump’s stillborn diesel deal: Why Russian oil tankers are not heading to the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e0d367dcba6ec6a3edbb291d93434d2966a505a5412dbbebc452addc7fa9b05</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:38:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-stillborn-diesel-deal-why-russian-oil-tankers-are-not-heading-to-the-us" /><summary type="html">The first oil tankers scheduled to deliver Russian diesel to the US under a deal between President Donald Trump and his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin have changed course and are no longer heading toward the US coast. It spells the end of an agreement announced with great fanfare before the midterms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Is Israel opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot going to replace Benjamin Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6119779b2af8691245d0e643d45393a873c62a45644ccce0698960ab9350eab8</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:25:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-is-israel-opposition-figure-gadi-eisenkot-going-to-replace-benjamin-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">In Israel, Gadi Eisenkot emerged on Thursday, November 5, as the frontrunner to be tasked with forming a government. This comes after one of the two main parties representing ultra-Orthodox Jewish voters – a longtime ally of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's coalition – declined to recommend any candidate for the task. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future in question after midterms setback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bb2e3ed37d1963db7e14630c8e59dda34c3baa9b3c181a396f4f4bc73494e14</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:15:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-us-defence-secretary-pete-hegseth-s-future-in-question-after-midterms-setback" /><summary type="html">US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future is in question after Tuesday's, November 3, midterms setback. On Thursday, November 5, he issued a video message vowing to fight efforts in Congress to impeach him and defending the ‌Iran war as “courageous and historic”. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech giants lose $1 trillion in one day after Democrats victory in midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01ba272181e83f6da94cfcd0dafca0f560bf7a0faf75f4c949e2b16792df1672</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:15:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-tech-giants-lose-1-trillion-in-one-day-after-democrats-victory-in-midterms" /><summary type="html">Trillions of dollars have been wiped off the stock value of major tech firms in the US, Europe and Asia. Investors appear worried about the possibility of an AI slowdown and tougher regulation as Democrats won the midterms in the US. Some of the Democratic candidates had expressed their opposition to the data centres that are needed to power AI technology.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canada PM Mark Carney unveils budget to strengthen economy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9706825f17e23df1911662cf9a02f8c2a0d06be69e2206049f33fc7b666e399</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:10:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-canada-pm-mark-carney-unveils-budget-to-strengthen-economy" /><summary type="html">Canada's Prime Minister Mark Carney unveiled his first ever budget on November 5, which set out strong ambitions for greater economic independence from the US. The "Masters of our Destiny" budget also announced generous measures for parts of the economy affected by tariffs, setting aside 44 billion Canadian dollars for impacted businesses and workers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Democratic Party introduce a new 'New Deal'? Key narrative must be 'focused on economic issues'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d96ba854fee582896b5daac6a411899edd364d7ea3ddc53f2519abcf4c8860f5</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:07:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/will-democratic-party-introduce-a-new-new-deal-key-narrative-must-be-focused-on-economic-issues" /><summary type="html">With Democrats poised to control both chambers of Congress, the party faces a defining challenge: how to constrain Donald Trump's presidency while carving out a path to the White House in 2028. For Ian Reifowitz, Distinguished Professor of History at SUNY Empire State University, the answer lies in drawing on the historical legacy of Franklin D. Roosevelt's New Deal coalition. Republicans, he argues, have progressively shifted electoral competition towards questions of identity, immigration and cultural conflict. Democrats, by contrast, must recover their traditional strength on economic security, affordability and everyday living standards. "These Democrats across the country ran on affordability." And that's how they must govern, explains Reifowitz.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Period of uncertainty: Trump is tormented, he's unstoppable, and he's desperate for immortality'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d3b2dceb58339303c7f5b4c40714e9d2e8aaf4caaf8f6a3422734c71b694064</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:46:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-period-of-uncertainty-trump-is-tormented-he-s-unstoppable-and-he-s-desperate-for-immortality" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Craig Copetas, Greek-American author, international affairs columnist and editor at Türkiye Today and French Senator Hélène Conway-Mouret. “What you have is a tormented and unstable president who's desperate for immortality.” With this arresting assessment, Copetas captures what he considers the defining paradox of Donald Trump's presidency in the aftermath of the US midterm elections: a leader politically neutered at home but potentially emboldened on the international stage.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>The human cost of recycling: Kenyan waste pickers put their health at risk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6128e63a54c45f89c0d7624123e546f9fdeae6da98ba1e883112fe9d3ba7a5bf</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:34:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261106-the-human-cost-of-recycling-kenyan-waste-pickers-put-their-health-at-risk" /><summary type="html">Two thousand tonnes of waste are dumped every day at the Dandora landfill site in the Kenyan capital Nairobi. An army of workers then rush in to recover recyclable materials, putting their own health at risk in the process. But however hard these unsung environmental heroes work, only 7 percent of the plastic can be recycled. Our correspondents report.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Europe's crisis of discontent: Student and cost-of-living protests spread across EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:787ab96b693e7ad6fdef8c34b9f35da608bd47f33a959e09fb8385cd3ea3a457</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T11:48:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261106-europe-s-crisis-of-discontent-student-and-cost-of-living-protests-spread-across-eu" /><summary type="html">A growing wave of discontent is sweeping across Europe. What began in France as student protests over deteriorating school conditions, teacher shortages and an education system under pressure has quickly grown into something much bigger: a groundswell of discontent over the rising cost of living, unaffordable housing and struggling public services.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Eisenkot claims 'progress' in coalition talks as opposition eases on ultra-Orthodox draft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07ee3d94bedca1ed898fd7f2b112324997597a34dced4875ea51a0b2b3c7a1e6</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T11:43:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261106-israel-s-eisenkot-claims-significant-progress-in-coalition-talks-as-opposition-eases-on-ultra-orthodox-draft" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot said on Friday he was making "significant progress" in forming a government to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu as one of his possible coalition partners walked back demands that ultra-Orthodox Jews complete military service and signalled a willingness to hold talks with the community.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>French 2027 presidential elections: Why Melenchon is a Gen Z favourite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7238bcf6721ee76c53b1b1c6a81b03409f97ed66c60b7cb4067b4bfabc02cd63</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T11:43:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-2027-presidential-elections-why-melenchon-is-a-gen-z-favourite" /><summary type="html">Hard-left presidential candidate Jean-Luc Melenchon is beloved by French youth, but also one of the country’s most controversial politicians. His encouragement of the youth protests sweeping through France months ahead of the presidential election has only made him more divisive. So, why is Melenchon a Gen Z favourite? FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler spoke to young supporters to find out.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms over, Democrats eye wide-open 2028 White House race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8f20349534b37e727fdc60142a162dbab95e05029ca4294156ceb822eb59e75</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:42:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-midterms-over-democrats-eye-wide-open-2028-white-house-race" /><summary type="html">With the US midterms over, Democrats are turning to what could become one of their most crowded and unpredictable presidential primaries in decades, a 2028 contest ​likely to expose the party's divide over how to win back the White House. Despite their resounding victories on Tuesday, Democrats enter the 2028 campaign still divided over whether to tack to the center or move further left on issues ranging from healthcare and taxes to policing and foreign policy.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel president to announce Sunday who will form new government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f783e1f34922dedeca8df6a22dc74cfd5f70f3d2c0c36135e9e33528df3493f</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:39:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-israel-president-to-announce-sunday-who-will-form-new-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog said he will announce on Sunday, November 8, whom he will task with trying to form a new government, following post-election talks with all party leaders. 46 parliament members recommended Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, while 67 backed his opponent Gadi Eisenkot. Seven lawmakers abstained.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Republicans face reckoning after major midterm election defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ffb9b0e85663e9d4f0aa2d203ea44c03548930d07e59452f80cc381d116478c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:37:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-us-republicans-face-reckoning-after-major-midterm-election-defeat" /><summary type="html">Following the Democrats' sweeping victory in Tuesday's US midterm elections, Republicans are facing a moment of reckoning. With Donald Trump now a "lame-duck" president, the party must find a way forward after a historic electoral setback. The GOP faces major questions about how to win back voters and who will lead the party, with the next presidential election just two years away.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least two killed, 23 injured in school bus accident in eastern France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f337922eaefa86bde22df0d290514efb30a5522c8048262178184bb4515136f</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:37:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261106-at-least-two-killed-16-injured-in-school-bus-accident-in-eastern-france" /><summary type="html">A bus carrying school children crashed south of Bourg-en-Bresse in eastern France on Friday, killing at least two people and injuring 23 others. The vehicle was carrying 43 passengers in total.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Pollution, shortages, crime: Daily life in Pakistan's megacity Karachi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8247e7d29d3a913bac0ffb3a6a5e0db1b6613365013e20d910791bef0f0871d6</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:32:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261106-pollution-shortages-crime-daily-life-in-pakistan-s-megacity-karachi" /><summary type="html">Fed up with hours of power cuts, the residents of Pakistan's economic hub Karachi took to the streets in recent days and blocked several major roads. The outburst of anger highlights the daily problems faced by a megacity of over 21 million people, which has once again been ranked among the world's least liveable cities.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Death toll rises to 50 in Russian attack on aid distribution ‌point in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73deaadee66b9bdfe17c754dbd03727701479da070da744b75157bd3eb2f7b0c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:15:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261106-death-toll-rises-to-50-in-russian-attack-on-aid-distribution-point-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">The death toll from Russia's bombing of an aid ​distribution ‌point in ⁠Ukraine's southeastern Zaporizhzhia region on Monday ‌has risen to 50, Kyiv's Emergency Service said on Friday, making it ​one of the deadliest strikes ‌on civilians this year.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
